<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">reload</ansi>

Chamber or nock a fresh projectile into the ranged weapon you have
equipped, readying it to fire. Reloading draws one round of ammunition
from a matching bundle in your pack (arrows for a bow, bolts for a
crossbow, shot for a sling, and so on).

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">reload</ansi>     Ready your equipped ranged weapon.

A ranged weapon must be loaded before it can be fired. If you have a
ranged weapon in either hand, it is reloaded automatically. Reloading
takes a moment and shares a cooldown with other special moves, so plan
your shots; you cannot reload again until it recovers.

Reloading is physical exertion that spends Stamina and requires full payment.
Carried load raises the price, while <ansi fg="skill">ranged-combat</ansi> skill
lowers it. If you are too spent, no ammunition or cooldown is consumed and the
weapon remains unchanged.

You need matching ammunition in your pack. When a bundle runs dry you
will be told it was your last.

<ansi fg="yellow">Reloading costs you an ambush:</ansi>

A shot fired from hiding is an <ansi fg="magenta-bold">ambush</ansi>, and it draws
on the very same recovery that reloading just spent. If you reload and then
hide, your special move is usually still coming back when you fire, so you
fire an ordinary shot instead and are told there was no ambush ready.

That shot still gives your position away. Firing from hiding reveals you
whether the ambush was ready or not, so a wasted opener costs you your cover
and returns nothing for it.

Load first, then hide, and give the recovery time to return before you shoot.
Check it with <ansi fg="command">cooldowns</ansi>. See <ansi fg="command">help ambush</ansi>.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help shoot</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help ranged-combat</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help stamina</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help equip</ansi>,
